{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"Layout","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI6LayoutP","roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Layout"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Layout"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that defines the geometry of a collection of views."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Associated Types","anchor":"Associated-Types","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/Cache"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/callAsFunction(_:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/explicitAlignment(of:in:proposal:subviews:cache:)-1jge4","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/explicitAlignment(of:in:proposal:subviews:cache:)-2hh6p","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/makeCache(subviews:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/placeSubviews(in:proposal:subviews:cache:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/sizeThatFits(proposal:subviews:cache:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/spacing(subviews:cache:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/updateCache(_:subviews:)"]},{"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/Subviews"]},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/layoutProperties"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/layout"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Layout","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You traditionally arrange views in your app’s user interface using built-in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout containers like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HStack"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Grid"},{"type":"text","text":". If you need more complex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout behavior, you can define a custom layout container by creating a type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that conforms to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Layout"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol and implementing its required"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"methods:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/sizeThatFits(proposal:subviews:cache:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports the size of the composite layout view."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/placeSubviews(in:proposal:subviews:cache:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assigns positions to the container’s subviews.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can define a basic layout type with only these two methods:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["struct BasicVStack: Layout {","    func sizeThatFits(","        proposal: ProposedViewSize,","        subviews: Subviews,","        cache: inout ()","    ) -> CGSize {","        \/\/ Calculate and return the size of the layout container.","    }","","    func placeSubviews(","        in bounds: CGRect,","        proposal: ProposedViewSize,","        subviews: Subviews,","        cache: inout ()","    ) {","        \/\/ Tell each subview where to appear.","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use your layout the same way you use a built-in layout"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"container, by providing a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ViewBuilder"},{"type":"text","text":" with the list of subviews"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to arrange:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["BasicVStack {","    Text(\"A Subview\")","    Text(\"Another Subview\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Support additional behaviors","level":3,"anchor":"Support-additional-behaviors","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can optionally implement other protocol methods and properties to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provide more layout container features:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Define explicit horizontal and vertical layout guides for the container by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implementing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"explicitAlignment(of:in:proposal:subviews:cache:)-8ofeu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"explicitAlignment(of:in:proposal:subviews:cache:)-3iqmu"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"respectively."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Establish the preferred spacing around the container by implementing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spacing(subviews:cache:)-86z2e"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Indicate the axis of orientation for a container that has characteristics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of a stack by implementing the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"layoutProperties-5rb5b"},{"text":" static property.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Create and manage a cache to store computed values across different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"layout protocol calls by implementing ","type":"text"},{"code":"makeCache(subviews:)-23agy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol provides default implementations for these symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"if you don’t implement them. See each method or property for details.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Add input parameters","level":3,"anchor":"Add-input-parameters","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can define parameters as inputs to the layout, like you might","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["struct BasicVStack: Layout {","    var alignment: HorizontalAlignment","","    \/\/ ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set the parameters at the point where you instantiate the layout:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["BasicVStack(alignment: .leading) {","    \/\/ ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the layout provides default values for its parameters, you can omit the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameters at the call site, but you might need to keep the parentheses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after the name of the layout, depending on how you specify the defaults.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For example, suppose you set a default alignment for the basic stack in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the parameter declaration:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["struct BasicVStack: Layout {","    var alignment: HorizontalAlignment = .center","","    \/\/ ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To instantiate this layout using the default center alignment, you don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have to specify the alignment value, but you do need to add empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parentheses:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["BasicVStack() {","    \/\/ ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift compiler requires the parentheses in this case because of how the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout protocol implements this call site syntax. Specifically, the layout’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/callAsFunction(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method looks for an initializer with exactly zero"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input arguments when you omit the parentheses from the call site."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can enable the simpler call site for a layout that doesn’t have an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implicit initializer of this type by explicitly defining one:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["init() {","    self.alignment = .center","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For information about Swift initializers, see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Initialization.html"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift Programming Language"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Interact with subviews through their proxies","level":3,"anchor":"Interact-with-subviews-through-their-proxies","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To perform layout, you need information about all of its subviews, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the views that your container arranges. While your layout can’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interact directly with its subviews, it can access a set of subview proxies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/Subviews"},{"type":"text","text":" collection that each protocol method receives as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an input parameter. That type is an alias for the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubviews"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection type, which in turn contains "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview"},{"type":"text","text":" instances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that are the subview proxies."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can get information about each subview from its proxy, like its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimensions and spacing preferences. This enables"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you to measure subviews before you commit to placing them. You also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"assign a position to each subview by calling its proxy’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/place(at:anchor:proposal:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Call the method on each subview from within your implementation of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/placeSubviews(in:proposal:subviews:cache:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Access layout values","level":3,"anchor":"Access-layout-values","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Views have layout values that you set with view modifiers.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Layout containers can choose to condition their behavior accordingly.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For example, a built-in ","type":"text"},{"code":"HStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" allocates space to its subviews based","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in part on the priorities that you set with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/layoutPriority(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view modifier. Your layout container accesses this value for a subview by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reading the proxy’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/priority","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" property.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also create custom layout values by creating a layout key."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Set a value on a view with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/layoutValue(key:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"modifier. Read the corresponding value from the subview’s proxy using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key as an index on the subview. For more information about creating,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"setting, and accessing custom layout values, see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutValueKey"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/LayoutSubviews":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/layoutsubviews","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubviews","title":"LayoutSubviews","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayoutSubviews","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LayoutSubviews"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A collection of proxy values that represent the subviews of a layout view.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Layout/callAsFunction(_:)":{"title":"callAsFunction(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/callAsFunction(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/layout\/callasfunction(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Combines the specified views into a single composite view using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the layout algorithms of the custom layout container.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"callAsFunction","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"V"},{"kind":"text","text":">(() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"V"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{